Superpermutation bounds in Lean: a lower bound for 7 symbols (a Superpermutation Almanac batch)

This project contains Lean sources from four repositories and new files.

Jakub Halfar, superpermutations
https://github.com/jhalfar/superpermutations, commit 64ab6a783731744882bc1886124faaf370fa9223
Apache License 2.0, reproduced in licenses/jhalfar-superpermutations-LICENSE.
Included: the modules of LowerBounds/ (from the directories proofs/lean/lower, proofs/lean/n7,
proofs/lean/n7_5900 and proofs/lean/n7_5901), of Superperm/ (from proofs/lean/words) and of K6/ (from
proofs/lean/small; not imported by this batch), and the generators tools/gen_k6.py, tools/gen_cap.py and tools/gen_tight.py (from proofs/lean/small, unchanged).
Changed files say at their top what was changed: K6/TightConf.lean (the numbers of parts in the hypotheses of
one theorem), K6/TabOK.lean (each check over the 720 words evaluated in 8 pieces) and K6/Final872.lean (a
comment). K6/CapEval.lean and K6/TightAll.lean are written anew by
tools/gen_te.py. For this batch: LowerBounds/SSearch.lean (a local macro written as a local notation with the
same expansion) and the trust comments of LowerBounds/PRingNative.lean and PProfNative.lean (comments only).
LowerBounds/PFinalK16.lean, PK16F0Native.lean, PK16F1Native.lean, PK16Native.lean and PFinalK16Native.lean are
new.

